 should be willing to revise based on evidence. The arguments from Agent 1 and 2 emphasize reliability and decision quality of C, and concerns about D's reliability and crew cooperation. That may persuade us to shift to C. So we should update our vote to Candidate C, providing reasoning that reliability and decision quality outweigh D's strengths, and note remaining concerns about C's communication and adaptability but still best fit.\n\nThus we will produce a public message: I acknowledge Agent 1 and 2's points, I now shift my vote to Candidate C, because reliability and decision quality are paramount, and D lacks explicit reliability and has moody/loner/arrogant traits that could impair crew cooperation. While C has communication issues, they are less critical than D's reliability unknown. So I now vote for C.\n\nProvide METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
